summary:
- University: Hong Kong Polytechnic University
- Department: Department of Computing
- Project: EnergyKnow: Knowledge-driven smart building energy management with heterogeneous energy systems
- Duties: Assist the project leader in developing and integrating knowledge-graph and AI methods for heterogeneous building-energy data; build load/renewable-generation forecasting and PV–ESS–HVAC energy optimisation/control models; implement data pipelines, Python APIs and visualisation; deploy and evaluate the integrated platform at an external trial site; prepare technical reports, demonstrations, and research publications; perform any other duties as assigned;
- Requirements: Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Electrical/Energy Engineering, Building Services Engineering or a related discipline; at least three years of postdoctoral research experience or equivalent qualifications and experience; strong Python/programming and research skills, experience in graphs/ontologies, machine learning, optimisation/control, time-series forecasting, BMS/HVAC, PV or ESS;
- Appointment: Twelve months
- Conditions: Competitive remuneration package; consideration of applications commences on 22 September 2026 until the position is filled;
- Contact: Applicants can contact Prof. Zhang Chen at telephone number 2766 4901 or via email at jason-c.zhang@polyu.edu.hk for further information;
- Closing date: 2026-09-22
- Key requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Electrical/Energy Engineering, Building Services Engineering or a related discipline; at least three years of postdoctoral research experience or equivalent qualifications and experience; strong Python/programming and research skills, experience in graphs/ontologies, machine learning, optimisation/control, time-series forecasting, BMS/HVAC, PV or ESS;
- Main duties: Develop and integrate knowledge-graph and AI methods for heterogeneous building-energy data; Build load/renewable-generation forecasting and PV–ESS–HVAC energy optimisation/control models; Implement data pipelines,
